            <ArticleTitle>[Pain and fear in animals].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>69-70</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Pain and fear are feelings of reluctance, which result in a behaviour of avoidance. They are protective mechanisms and are only partly approachable to the quantification with natural scientific methods. It will pointed to the central role of the diencephalon, limbic system and the cerebral cortex concerning the processing and valuation of mental state. The recognition of clinical symptoms and precise behavioural observations are an essential aid to assess the state of pain and fear in animals.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
